The [companies page](/companies) now filters by industry. Pick **Fintech** and you get
2 016 companies; **Healthcare** gives 7 423. Before today that filter existed only for
companies in the Y Combinator directory, which is a small slice of the catalogue.

### Why it took a rewrite rather than a checkbox

The industry field was already there. The problem was what it held: two different
vocabularies stacked on top of each other, so `AI` and `Artificial Intelligence` sat
side by side as separate values, along with `FinTech` against `Fintech` and leftovers
from an old import like `Tech, Software & IT Services`. A filter built on that would
have split every industry across several entries and quietly missed companies under
whichever spelling you did not click.

So the field now runs through one curated list of 74 industries. Anything outside it
is not stored — no guessing, no inventing a category from a label nobody agreed on.
105 212 companies carry at least one industry today.

### Also on company pages

While the catalogue was open we filled two gaps that had nothing to do with filtering:

- **16 601 companies** gained a link to their actual website, where there was none before.
- **9 858 companies** gained a short description.

Existing descriptions and links were left alone — the new data only filled blanks.
